%global debug_package %{nil}
Name: buskill-vm
Version: @VERSION@
Release: @REL@%{?dist}

Summary: BusKill laptop kill cord for QubesOS (VM package)
License: GPLv3+
URL: https://www.buskill.in/

Source0: %{name}-%{version}.tar.gz

BuildRequires: make

%description
BusKill is a laptop kill cord. When the USB cable's magnetic breakaway is
severed, it triggers your computer to lock, shutdown, or shred its LUKS
encryption keys -- keeping your encrypted data safe from thieves.

This package installs the udev rules and scripts for the sys-usb VM in
QubesOS. Install this package in the TemplateVM used by your sys-usb qube.

After installing this package, you must also install the buskill-dom0 package
in dom0 to configure the qrexec services.

%prep
%setup -q

%install
make install-vm DESTDIR=$RPM_BUILD_ROOT

%files
%attr(0644, root, root) /etc/udev/rules.d/70-buskill.rules
%attr(0644, root, root) /usr/lib/qubes-buskill/vm/buskill.rules
%attr(0644, root, root) /usr/lib/qubes-buskill/vm/buskill.lock.rules
%attr(0755, root, root) /usr/lib/qubes-buskill/vm/buskill-disarm.sh

%changelog
@CHANGELOG@
